{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"Local profiling shows concurrency should be conditional: it helps from `seq_len=256` upward but its event overhead hurts the shortest shapes. One auxiliary stream is faster than two, and GELU tile sizes have clear shape-dependent optima. I’m folding those measured choices in, while reusing the now-dead `grad_gelu` buffer for the exact post-GELU result."}}
